<BaseLayout title="Personality Development Workshop" description="Personality development workshop conducted by Sarvagun Society at Ghuttu Inter College, Tehri Garhwal for over 120 students.">
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--spacing-page)] px-4 lg:px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-heading font-bold mb-6">Personality Development Workshop in Ghuttu (Tehri)</h1>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-text-muted space-y-4">
        <p><strong>Date:</strong> 23 July 2010</p>
        <p><strong>Venue:</strong> Ghuttu Inter College, village Ghuttu, Tehri Garhwal</p>

        <p>Pauri Garhwal Group of Delhi organized a program in Ghuttu Inter College — one of the last Inter Colleges of India in Uttarakhand. Members from Sarvagun Society, Dehradun were invited to conduct a workshop on Personality Development.</p>

        <p>The strength of students in Ghuttu Inter College is nearly 600. During morning assembly, the Principal introduced The Sarvagun Society and its resource people. Students performed morning prayer and a welcome song.</p>

        <p>Mr. Rahul Rawat, Secretary of The Sarvagun Society, discussed the life and ideas of Swami Vivekananda. Students of classes 11th and 12th were divided into groups, each assigned a resource person for a personality development class.</p>

        <p>More than <strong>120 students</strong> participated. They were taught meditation — for most, it was their first encounter with the practice. After meditation, group discussions, brain storming, and other group activities were conducted.</p>

        <p>An interaction session followed where students asked questions about career, IQ, and EQ. Students felt motivated to do better in their future.</p>

        <p>The Principal, students, and teachers highly appreciated the workshops and invited the society to visit again.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
